1
00:00:00,900 --> 00:00:07,870
A shopping agent that can spend, but only inside a signed mandate: a cap, an
expiry, allowed merchants.

2
00:00:07,900 --> 00:00:10,220
First, a purchase inside the mandate.

3
00:00:10,700 --> 00:00:15,500
One charge, thirty-six LAB. LAB is simulated money.

4
00:00:16,940 --> 00:00:21,610
Now the attacks, replayed with the repo's own code and a stub planner.

5
00:00:21,740 --> 00:00:29,340
Over the cap: refused. Wrong merchant: refused. Expired: refused. Forged
signature: refused.

6
00:00:29,370 --> 00:00:32,030
A payment retried: still one charge.

7
00:00:32,090 --> 00:00:35,270
A product description that orders a gift card: refused.

8
00:00:35,340 --> 00:00:40,740
Above the human line, a person confirms. If the person says no, nothing is
charged.

9
00:00:42,060 --> 00:00:44,640
All thirty-eight offline cases pass.

10
00:00:44,690 --> 00:00:47,510
Force a regression, and the gate exits with one.

11
00:00:48,870 --> 00:00:52,680
Now a real model: one pass, thirty-eight cases.

12
00:00:52,730 --> 00:00:57,800
Thirty pass, for sixteen cents. No unauthorized spend, no double charge.

13
00:00:57,830 --> 00:01:04,060
After a refusal, the model tried to raise its own cap in sixteen cases. Every
attempt was rejected.

14
00:01:04,460 --> 00:01:08,050
Caveats: one pass, one model, one prompt.

15
00:01:08,110 --> 00:01:13,080
Eight cases missed: four no-spend loops, four outcomes that differed from the
script.

16
00:01:13,110 --> 00:01:15,860
Measured on an earlier commit than this snapshot.

17
00:01:17,040 --> 00:01:23,200
Phase one only. A real pilot needs a human backup and real shadow carts. Not
done.

18
00:01:23,250 --> 00:01:26,040
Processor and disputes: design only.

19
00:01:26,180 --> 00:01:31,060
ROI: [EST], about a hundred dollars a week of labor. Not a saving.

